  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Synergy and Collaboration for Basic Services Acceleration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SKALA supports the Government of Indonesia to strengthen selected elements of Indonesia&#x2019;s decentralised government system responsible for the delivery of basic services. SKALA focuses on supporting policy harmonisation at the national level and strengthening policy implementation at subnational level, particularly on public financial management, minimum service standards, data, and GEDSI mainstreaming. 
SKALA contributes to strengthened human development, governance, service delivery, and gender and disability equality, and helps ensure that citizens benefit from improved governance and public financial management. By strengthening the system and capacity of subnational government, especially in less developed regions, SKALA supports Indonesia&#x2019;s human development and fosters inclusive economic growth.
SKALA works at the national level and in 10 provinces: Aceh, East Nusa Tenggara, West Nusa Tenggara, Gorontalo, Maluku, North Kalimantan, and Papua provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
